.TH GIT-UPDATER 1 "August 2026" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-updater \- Track git repos, pin commits, export vendor.lock, replicate stacks.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-updater
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR
[\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Track git repos, pin commits, export vendor.lock, replicate stacks.

Machine-readable help:
.P
.B git-updater --help-json
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-self-check
Skip automatic self-update check after command (default: False)
.TP
.B --help-json
Print machine-readable CLI spec as JSON and exit (default: False)
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
First-run setup: catalog, pip -e this clone, skills, adopt self, replicate shared.lock
.br
--root  Clone root (default: cwd; if cwd is this checkout, its parent)
.br
--force  Overwrite existing catalog
.br
--lock  Replicate this lock after init (default: examples/shared.lock if present)
.br
--no-lock  Skip stack lock replicate
.br
--no-pip  Skip pip install -e of this checkout
.TP
.B scan
List git repos under root not in catalog
.TP
.B add
Clone and register a repo
.br
repo (required) owner/repo, any git URL (https/ssh), file:// path, or local folder
.br
--name  Catalog name (default: repo name)
.br
--path  Relative path under root
.br
--branch  Branch to clone (default: main)
.br
--install  Override install hook (default: read .git-updater.yaml from repo)
.TP
.B adopt
Register an existing clone
.br
folder (required) Folder name or path under root
.br
--name  Catalog name
.br
--branch  Override branch
.br
--install  Override install hook (default: read .git-updater.yaml from repo)
.TP
.B sync-hooks
Refresh install/update hooks from each repo's .git-updater manifest
.br
name (optional) Single repo
.TP
.B rm
Remove from catalog (keeps folder)
.br
name (required) Catalog name
.TP
.B status
Show pin status
.br
name (optional) Single repo
.br
--fetch  Fetch before comparing remote
.TP
.B pin
Pin catalog to current HEAD
.br
name (optional) Single repo
.br
--export  Also write vendor.lock
.TP
.B install
Clone missing repos and run install hooks
.br
name (optional) Single repo
.TP
.B update
Fetch and fast-forward clean repos
.br
name (optional) Single repo
.TP
.B consolidate
Fetch and merge/rebase when update would fail; resolve conflicts stepwise
.br
name (optional) Single repo
.br
--rebase  Use rebase instead of merge when not fast-forwardable
.br
--continue  Continue after you fixed merge/rebase conflicts
.br
--abort  Abort an in-progress merge or rebase
.TP
.B push
Push tracking branch
.br
name (optional) Single repo
.TP
.B export
Write vendor.lock and VENDOR.md
.br
--out  Lock file path (default: <root>/vendor.lock)
.TP
.B replicate
Bootstrap stack from vendor.lock
.br
lockfile (required) Path to vendor.lock
.br
--root  Clone root on this machine (default: directory that contains the lockfile)
.br
--dry-run  Print actions without cloning
.TP
.B verify
Check clones match lock (exit 1 on drift)
.br
--lock  Lock file (default: <root>/vendor.lock)
.br
--root  Override root
.TP
.B self-check
Check whether git-updater itself is up to date
.br
--fetch  Fetch from origin / GitHub before comparing (bypasses 24h cache)
.br
--json  Also print machine-readable result
.TP
.B self-update
Fast-forward git-updater to latest upstream
.TP
.B install-skills
Copy the git-updater agent skill to ~/.cursor/skills and ~/.agents/skills
.TP
.B help
Show help; --json for the machine-readable spec
.br
topic (optional) Command name
.br
--json  Print CLI spec as JSON
.TP
.B man
Print man page (roff) to stdout
.br
--write  Write roff to this file instead of stdout
.SH FILES
~/.git-updater/catalog.json
.br
Machine-local catalog (clone root, pins).
.br
<clone-root>/vendor.lock
.br
Shareable SHA pins (relative paths only).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. Non-zero on error, verify drift, or self-check behind/dirty/diverged.
.SH SEE ALSO
git-updater --help, git-updater --help-json, git-updater man
